    "南锣鼓巷位于北京鼓楼与地安门之间，南北向，全长786米，宽约8米。所附资料称其与元大都同期形成，街巷两侧排列16条支巷，整体呈棋盘式里坊格局，并保存传统胡同与院落肌理。资料还记载，该巷旧称“罗锅巷”，1750年《全城全图》改称南锣鼓巷。现有材料同时描述其历史街区风貌与后来的商业、休闲活动。": {
      "en": "Nanluoguxiang is located between Beijing Drum Tower and Di’anmen, running north–south, with a total length of 786 meters and a width of approximately 8 meters. The accompanying materials state that it took shape during the same period as Dadu of the Yuan dynasty. Sixteen branch lanes line both sides of the street, which retains an overall checkerboard-style neighborhood layout as well as the traditional hutong and courtyard pattern. The materials also record that the lane was formerly called “Luoguoxiang” and was renamed Nanluoguxiang in the 1750 Complete Map of the City. The existing materials describe both the character of the historic district and its later commercial and leisure activities.",
      "confidence": "official",
      "source": "AI翻译"
    },
    "福祥胡同是南锣鼓巷西侧八条支巷之一，位于传统胡同片区内。2020年东城区相关报道将其列入整治修缮范围，称修缮后胡同肌理和院落风貌得到保留，同时改善了居民住房、厨卫及市政设施。现有资料所述重点是街巷整体更新和居民生活环境，未提供福祥胡同单独的长度、宽度或具体历史建筑清单。": {
      "en": "Fuxiang Hutong is one of the eight branch lanes on the west side of Nanluoguxiang, within a traditional hutong area. A 2020 report concerning Dongcheng District included it in the scope of renovation and restoration, stating that the hutong pattern and courtyard character were retained after the work, while residents’ housing, kitchen and bathroom facilities, and municipal infrastructure were improved. The existing materials focus on the overall renewal of the lane and residents’ living environment and do not provide Fuxiang Hutong’s individual length, width, or a specific list of historic buildings.",
      "confidence": "official",
      "source": "AI翻译"
    },
    "蓑衣胡同是南锣鼓巷西侧支巷之一。东城区融媒体转引的报道显示，蓑衣胡同与雨儿、帽儿、福祥三条胡同共同实施修缮整治，项目强调保留原有胡同肌理和院落风貌，并改善居民居住条件及公共环境。所附资料没有给出蓑衣胡同单独的历史沿革、尺度或院落名录。": {
      "en": "Suoyi Hutong is one of the branch lanes on the west side of Nanluoguxiang. A report reproduced by Dongcheng District’s integrated media states that Suoyi Hutong, Yuer Hutong, Mao’er Hutong, and Fuxiang Hutong underwent renovation and improvement together. The project emphasized retaining the original hutong pattern and courtyard character while improving residents’ living conditions and the public environment. The accompanying materials do not provide Suoyi Hutong’s individual historical development, dimensions, or a list of courtyards.",
      "confidence": "official",
      "source": "AI翻译"
    },
    "雨儿胡同是南锣鼓巷西侧支巷之一。现有报道记载，该胡同在整治修缮中保留胡同肌理和院落风貌，并改善居民住房、市政设施与公共环境。报道特别介绍雨儿胡同30号院：原为清朝值年旗衙门杂物房所在地，后部分腾退房间转作居民议事、公共活动、社区服务及展览展陈空间。资料另称齐白石曾居住在雨儿胡同13号。": {
      "en": "Yuer Hutong is one of the branch lanes on the west side of Nanluoguxiang. Existing reports record that the hutong’s pattern and courtyard character were retained during renovation and improvement, while residents’ housing, municipal facilities, and the public environment were improved. The reports specifically introduce Courtyard No. 30, formerly the site of a storeroom of the Qing dynasty banner office responsible for annual duty. Some vacated rooms were later converted into spaces for residents’ discussions, public activities, community services, and exhibitions. The materials also state that Qi Baishi once lived at No. 13 Yuer Hutong.",
      "confidence": "official",
      "source": "AI翻译"
    },
    "帽儿胡同位于北京老城区鼓楼与地安门之间，东西向，全长565米、宽7米。首都之窗资料称其清乾隆年间已称帽儿胡同，名称沿用至今，曾一度改称辉煌街四条后恢复原名。胡同内有可园及35、37号院等历史宅院：可园原为文煜住宅和花园，35、37号院曾为婉容娘家。现有资料强调相关宅院只能从外部看到院门，未说明内部常态开放。": {
      "en": "Mao’er Hutong is located between the Drum Tower and Di’anmen in Beijing’s old city, running east–west, with a total length of 565 meters and a width of 7 meters. Materials from the Capital Window state that it was already called Mao’er Hutong during the Qianlong period of the Qing dynasty. The name has continued to the present; it was temporarily changed to Fourth Huihuang Street before being restored. The hutong contains historic residences and gardens including Keyuan and Courtyards Nos. 35 and 37. Keyuan was formerly the residence and garden of Wenyu, while Courtyards Nos. 35 and 37 once belonged to Wanrong’s maternal family. Existing materials emphasize that the gates of these residences can only be viewed from outside and do not state that their interiors are regularly open.",
      "confidence": "official",
      "source": "AI翻译"
    },
    "景阳胡同被所附北京旅游网资料列为南锣鼓巷西侧八条支巷之一。现有来源未提供该胡同单独的长度、宽度、名称沿革、建筑名录或修缮详情，因此只能确认其在南锣鼓巷传统支巷体系中的身份，不能据整体街区资料补写本巷的专属历史。": {
      "en": "Jingyang Hutong is listed in the accompanying Beijing Tourism materials as one of the eight branch lanes on the west side of Nanluoguxiang. Existing sources provide no separate information on the hutong’s length, width, historical development of its name, building inventory, or renovation details. Its identity within the traditional branch-lane system of Nanluoguxiang can therefore be confirmed, but its specific history cannot be supplemented with information about the broader historic district.",
